From 32c8991b9cae61f418a2c231d665c6564fa77b8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:45:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Empty states for a member with no friends show the screen
 they become (rule 1680)

Owner-approved b58-empty-states.png, web and iPhone. Each empty state is a faded sample of the
full screen (the screen's own component with sample data, 32% opacity, inert and hidden from
accessibility), a title with the accent tick, one Newsreader line and one cream button:

- Social, People (Lately): a Blend tile beside Find, Lately faded with a sample post, "What
  friends are watching", Invite a friend (the invite drawer), quiet Find people.
- Blend: the tile opens "What's our Blend?" over a faded Blend; Blend with a friend opens the
  /m/handle link sheet; "They rate a few films they know to see it."
- Movie night alone: "Movie night takes two" over a faded lineup with % for the room; Send the
  link (share sheet); quiet Open the room anyway. Replaces "Send the link to start".
- Groups: "Pick films together", Start a group, "You'll get a link to send to your people."
- Chats: "Chats are with friends", Invite a friend.
- People, Following: "Follow your people", Invite a friend.

EmptyState gains `sample` (web and iPhone); FriendFeed takes sample rows; Blend exports
BlendSample; group and chat rows are extracted so the samples draw with them; useInviteDrawer
opens the invite drawer from Chats and People. Rule 1680 checks it all; rules 638, 831, 1265,
1298, 1331, 1336, 1369 and 1412 amended where they pinned the old copy. Swift not compiled here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013WRDCFXH8nihP92apJAVW7
