 1330. **"This account already exists": name it, count both sides, merge by default, Replace only after a confirm, web and iPhone** (owner-approved 2026-11-06, CS-Term-Project mockups/journeys/account-exists-v1.html Proposed, account-exists-v1-1-choice.png, -2-confirm.png and -3-after.png). When a guest (rule 996) or a signed-out reveal signs in with an Apple ID, Google account or email that already has a Montage account, the drawer (web `AccountExistsDrawer` in AccountExists.tsx, iPhone `AccountExistsPanel` in Features/SignIn/AccountExists.swift) shows the title "This account already exists" with the tick, the sign-in that matched as a chip (Apple ID / Google / Email and the address, never an Apple relay address), and one 12-radius panel: "Your account" (their photo, "@handle · Archetype", N ratings) over "This session" (two posters, "Archetype · just now", M ratings) and "K films are rated on both." Then the cream "Keep my account, add these ratings" with "RECOMMENDED Adds X. Where you rated a film twice, your account's rating stays.", the outline "Keep my account only" with "This session's M ratings are discarded.", a quiet red "Replace my account with this session" (only when the account has ratings) and a quiet Cancel (× too). Replace opens "Replace your account?": the red circle, what is deleted and moved, the ledger (Deleted from your account N ratings in red / Moved in from this session M ratings / Stays: sign-in, @handle, followers), "I understand my N ratings will be deleted." to tick, then the red outline "Delete N ratings and replace" (dim until ticked) and Back. After add or replace the receipt toast: "Added 22 ratings to @handle" / "8 you'd rated before kept your account's stars. 434 rated now." **Server** (`POST /api/account-merge`, lib/account-merge.ts `planMerge`): the account is the verified bearer (never a guest); a guest session is proved only by its own access token, taken before the switch and checked with Supabase Auth (`auth.getUser`, must be anonymous and not the account); a signed-out reveal's session is its finished, unclaimed quiz job under a week old, which only ever writes into the caller's own account; no user id is read from the body. `add` writes the session's films the account has no stars for as in-app rows (source "merge"), never touching a rated film, plus a guest's watchlist and Not interested, with no ledger events, then rebuilds the taste read (`maybeNudgeIdentity`); it is idempotent. `replace` needs `expect` equal to the account's rated count now, deletes the account's in-app ratings and un-seen marks and puts the session's build and library on the account's profile row (id, handle, photo, followers and sign-in stay). **The replace backup** (owner-approved 2026-11-07): before anything is deleted, `saveReplaceBackup` (lib/replace-backup.ts) copies the account's user_ratings rows, its un-seen (`rating`) marks, the "hidden" marks the replace is about to add, and the row's previous `result_json` and `library_json` to ai_cache under `replace-backup:<profileId>:<ms>` (service role only); a failed backup stops the replace (500, nothing deleted), and a replace run again with nothing left to lose writes none. The new library is then set exactly through `replace_imported_library` (the library guards would otherwise merge the deleted ratings back into library_json). Backups retire after 30 days (cleanup `RETIRE` `["replace-backup:", 30]`), go with a deleted profile (lib/aicache-prune.ts) and at once on account deletion. `node scripts/ops-call.mjs restore-replace <profile> [backupId]` (`POST /api/ops/restore-replace`, operator only) restores the newest backup or the one named: ratings (a film rated again since keeps the newer rating), un-seen marks, the previous build and rated library (the current watchlist stays), the hidden marks the replace added taken back, then the taste read rebuilt; idempotent. The confirm carries one line under the ledger, web and iPhone: "Can't be undone in the app. Contact us within 30 days to recover (contact@montagefilm.app)." (muted meta, the address a mail link; the body no longer says "This can't be undone."), and the Privacy page's Retention says the replaced ratings are kept 30 days. Keep my account only writes nothing; the guest is left as before. Cancel puts a guest back (its kept refresh token) or signs the reveal out. **The iPhone race:** the reveal goes on to the handle step only once the profile read says the account is new (`auth.profileChecked && auth.profileId == nil`), and `holdsBuild` holds the reveal from its stash with or without its job, so an existing account never opens straight into its tabs with the build dropped. Amends rules 85, 1121, 1254 and 1298. No em dashes. Not built on the iPhone (Swift does not compile here); every changed line was read. Checked by `scripts/check-invariants.ts` (1330).
